      "message": "Deduping is worth having (CV retries failed builders on the same patchset, so a stale failure next to a passing retry would get triaged), but this could be a lot smaller:\n\n```\ndef _latest_blocking_attempts(builds):\n    \"\"\"Drops cq_experimental builds; keeps the newest attempt per builder.\"\"\"\n    latest \u003d {}\n    for b in sorted(builds, key\u003dlambda b: b[\"createTime\"]):\n        if {\"key\": \"cq_experimental\", \"value\": \"true\"} in b.get(\"tags\", []):\n            continue\n        builder \u003d b[\"builder\"]\n        latest[(builder[\"project\"], builder[\"bucket\"], builder[\"builder\"])] \u003d b\n    return list(latest.values())\n```\n\n- Always apply it and drop `--all-attempts` / `--include-experimental` along with the two parameters. Nothing in the stack uses them, and anyone who really needs raw attempts has Gerrit or `bb ls`.\n- Key on `(project, bucket, builder)` and order by `createTime` (`_fetch_tryjobs` already requests both), the same as `git_cl._filter_failed_for_retry()`.\n- Buildbucket tags are plain `{key, value}` pairs, so the `isinstance` and `.lower()` checks aren\u0027t needed.",
